From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP cut is a neighbor boundary for chunk status

Entity ticking needs every neighbor in radius 2 marked full. Packed-spawn
carve unloads the corridor, so west piles one chunk off the hole drop out
of ENTITY_TICKING even when their own tickets still demand it. East piles
sit outside the ring and keep ticking. Do not leave the loaded-bit set —
that bit means the chunk is readable. Count a registered cut as a finished
boundary only when promoting full-chunk status. isNeighbourFullLoaded stays
false. Not bot herding, not moving TNT. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/scheduling/NewChunkHolder.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/scheduling/NewChunkHolder.java
@@ -1136,12 +1136,37 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Status promotion only. A registered cut is a finished region boundary, so it
+     * satisfies the radius-2 neighbor requirement. {@link #isNeighbourFullLoaded}
+     * stays false — the hole is not loaded and must not be read as a chunk.
+     */
+    private long neighbourBitsForStatus() {
+        long bits = this.fullNeighbourChunksLoadedBitset;
+        if (this.world == null) {
+            return bits;
+        }
+        for (int dz = -NEIGHBOUR_RADIUS; dz <= NEIGHBOUR_RADIUS; ++dz) {
+            for (int dx = -NEIGHBOUR_RADIUS; dx <= NEIGHBOUR_RADIUS; ++dx) {
+                if ((dx | dz) == 0) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.YapRegionizerGap.blocksAddChunk(
+                        this.world, this.chunkX + dx, this.chunkZ + dz)) {
+                    bits |= (1L << getFullNeighbourIndex(dx, dz));
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        return bits;
+    }
+
     // must hold scheduling lock
